Package: bkmborrow
Type: Package
Title: Dynamic Historical Borrowing for Bayesian Kaplan-Meier Inference
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Yusuke", "Yamaguchi", email = "yamagubed@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements dynamic borrowing of historical survival data within
    the conjugate Bayesian Kaplan-Meier framework, in which daily discrete
    hazards receive independent beta priors. For each arm with historical
    data, a weight is determined from the standardized discrepancy between
    the historical and current posterior restricted mean survival times
    (RMSTs). The weight either discounts the historical daily event and
    event-free counts (RG-H) or is applied to the arm-level RMST as a normal
    power prior (RG-R). Historical data may be available for the control arm
    only, the treatment arm only, or both arms. Exact posterior moments of the
    RMST, posterior sampling, and design stage calibration of the tolerance,
    which determines the weight's tuning constant, over a prespecified range
    of harmful drift are provided.
